 "note": "Quick, Draw! tooth 6139754980573184, a mouth seen from the front with its teeth showing. Stroke 0 is the line of the upper lip across the top; stroke 1 is the outline of the mouth, down the left side, round the bottom of the lower lip and up the right side; stroke 2 is a dot near the top left; stroke 3 is the row of upper teeth; stroke 4 is the row of lower teeth. The film shows a man's mouth from the front, opening and closing as he talks. The drawing is placed by its two mouth corners (where the outline's sides meet the bottom of the upper teeth), so it moves and widens with the man's mouth while its height stays one size. The upper lip line, the upper teeth and the top of the outline stay as drawn. Everything below the corners (the lower teeth and the bottom of the outline) folds up toward the line between the corners by the pose value 'open' (1 is the doodle as drawn, a wide open mouth; near 0.2 is the mouth closed), so the lower jaw drops and rises at the frames where the man's mouth opens and closes.",
